Report #229: "Need even more playerbot insults to counter the
defaults--wanting other bots to react to [item links]"
('wow, i just got [link]')

Two halves.

Insults: the toxic and taunt pools sat at 152/153 lines against a
player who has heard all of them. This adds 50 new
suggest_something_toxic lines (placeholder-free -- the broadcast
send path, BroadcastHelper::BroadcastSuggestSomethingToxic, fills
no name placeholders) and 25 new taunt lines (<target> only, which
is what the say::taunt action sets). Data only, in
mod-playerbots/data/sql/playerbots/updates/
2026_08_31_01_ai_playerbot_insults_and_item_link_reactions.sql.

Item links: ChatReplyAction::ChatReplyDo routed a chat message
containing an item link straight into GenerateReplyMessage, where
the verb parser matches nothing and the bot answers from the
REPLY_NOT_UNDERSTAND pool ("how should i know %s"). New
HandleItemLinkReply runs before that fallback: any message
containing |Hitem (after the WTB / toxic-links / thunderfury
handlers) pulls from a new reply_item_link pool (%s = the poster,
%random_inventory_item_link = a bot-owned item so lines can brag
back) and answers in the channel the link was posted in (say ->
PlayerbotAI::Say, yell -> Yell, world -> SayToWorld, general
channel -> GENERAL, guild/party/raid -> SayToGuild/SayToParty/
SayToRaid); unknown channels return false and fall through to the
generic reply as before. No new chance config: the receive-side
gates in PlayerbotAI (1-in-5 for real-player messages, 1-in-21
for bot chatter) already cap how many bots answer, and the reply
pool selection itself is always-on by design, so an
ai_playerbot_texts_chance row would never be consulted on this
path.

Touches (module only): modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/Actions/
SayAction.h (declaration), modules/mod-playerbots/src/Ai/Base/
Actions/SayAction.cpp (call site after the thunderfury handler +
handler), and the SQL update file above. No core files, no DBC.
